# generated diagrams (xo-deps.svg, xo-loc.svg, ..) are build output
*.svg
# .. but docs assets are source.  Without these, a figure committed in .rst with an
# untracked .svg builds green and 404s on the published site: sphinx only warns.
!**/docs/_static/img/*.svg
!_static/img/*.svg
**/utest/__pycache__
compile_commands.json
result
.build*
.cache
.projectile
.xo-backlog

# etc/host{egl,ubuntu}/ are GENERATED by etc/gen-hostegl from the committed
# .known basename lists.  They are host-specific -- they name driver builds
# that apt and nvidia bump underneath them -- so committing them means
# committing symlinks that dangle on every machine but the one that made them.
etc/hostegl/
etc/hostubuntu/
